# openapi-generator reads this file from its output directory, the repository root, and
# overwrites every file it emits under it, never deleting anything it does not. Unlike the Go
# generator, the Python one writes its packaging scaffold here beside the package, so this
# file is the only thing standing between a generation run and the hand-written files.
#
# Verified by running the generator into an empty directory with no ignore file: it writes the
# twelve root paths below. Three of them are hand-written in this repository; the other nine
# are scaffolding it never wants, kept out by the entry alone. All twelve are load-bearing.
#
# This file is what api-codegen's generate-python-sdk.sh compares its PROTECTED array against,
# whole line for whole line; AGENTS.md documents this list entry for entry. A variant spelling
# still protects the file but fails that check.

# Hand-written at the root: packaging, the repository README and the ignore rules.
pyproject.toml
README.md
.gitignore

# Suppressed rather than protected: the generator's setuptools/poetry/tox/CI scaffolding,
# which a uv project has no use for (this repository's workflow is test.yml). None of these
# exists in the tree, and CI asserts that.
.github/workflows/python.yml
setup.py
setup.cfg
requirements.txt
test-requirements.txt
tox.ini
.gitlab-ci.yml
.travis.yml
git_push.sh

# Hand-written inside the package: client construction and credentials, and the pagination
# helper. Defensive: the generator names its package files api_client.py, api_response.py,
# configuration.py, exceptions.py, rest.py, __init__.py and py.typed, and writes under api/
# and models/.
montecarlo/auth.py
montecarlo/oauth.py
montecarlo/profile.py
montecarlo/paging.py
